parameters.text:
=Section Title: {{ $('Split Out').item.json.title }}

Section Description: {{ $('Split Out').item.json.description }}

Newsletter Target Audience: {{ $('On form submission').item.json['Target Audience'] }}

Newsletter Tone: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.Tone }}

Please write the complete content for this newsletter section. Research the topic thoroughly using the tavily tool, then write engaging, well-researched content that:
1. Matches the section description
2. Is tailored to the target audience
3. Maintains the specified tone
4. Includes inline hyperlinked citations for all sources
5. Is approximately 200-300 words

=Format the following newsletter sections into a single HTML newsletter. 

Section Titles: {{ $json.data.map(item => item.title).join(', ') }}
Section Content: {{ $json.data.map(item => item.output).join('\n\n') }}

TARGET AUDIENCE: {{ $('On form submission').item.json['Target Audience'] }}
TONE: {{ $('On form submission').item.json.Tone }}

Instructions:
1. Combine all sections into one newsletter
2. Use <h2> for each section title
3. Keep all citations and hyperlinks
4. Add Sources section at the end
5. Stay under 750 words

Output ONLY this JSON structure, nothing else:
{
  "output": "<h2>Title</h2><p>content...</p>...<h2>Sources</h2><ul>...</ul>"
}

=Create a compelling newsletter title for this HTML newsletter:

{{ $json.output }}

Output only the title in plain text. No quotes, no explanation.

parameters.jsCode:
let data = items[0].json.output;

// If it's a JSON string, parse it
if (typeof data === 'string' && data.includes('"output"')) {
  try {
    const parsed = JSON.parse(data);
    data = parsed.output;
  } catch (e) {
    // Fallback: extract with regex
    const match = data.match(/"output":\s*"([\s\S]*)"\s*}/);
    data = match ? match[1] : data;
  }
}

// Unescape special characters
if (typeof data === 'string') {
  data = data
    .replace(/\\n/g, '\n')
    .replace(/\\"/g, '"')
    .replace(/\\\//g, '/');
}

return [{ json: { output: data } }];
